{"id": "EUVD-2026-86300", "enisaUuid": "3cf64ce4-e622-3afe-8b1a-4f84758f763f", "description": "Discourse is an open-source discussion platform. Prior to 2026.1.8, 2026.6.3, 2026.7.2, and 2026.8.0, the iframe src traversal guard did not treat literal backslashes as path separators after decoded dot segments. A crafted source could therefore pass an allowed_iframes subpath check while browser URL normalization moved the iframe outside the intended allowed path. The resulting iframe could load content from a location that the administrator did not allow. This issue is fixed in versions 2026.1.8, 2026.6.3, 2026.7.2, and 2026.8.0.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:54:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T17:11:34", "baseScore": 7.2, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N", "references": ["https://github.com/discourse/discourse/security/advisories/GHSA-6pwj-wgg8-4rjc", "https://github.com/discourse/discourse/pull/42882", "https://github.com/discourse/discourse/commit/042d7b159beda4f74d23e245e8b2e396d9ff8318", "https://github.com/discourse/discourse/commit/097ce5600a2d74d9c68e57974597ab2684bd2a24", "https://github.com/discourse/discourse/commit/0b5a27e689925edce9ba9b14110022435d2b94be", "https://github.com/discourse/discourse/commit/142f5155ad8e56ddb8012c4e70c69a03dedc0579"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-91123"], "assigner": "GitHub_M", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1687b657-42ac-30ef-8db6-e3fc3d99021e", "product": {"name": "discourse", "vendor": {"name": "discourse"}}, "product_version": "< 2026.8.0"}, {"id": "32d2daa1-68a8-30e8-833e-3d9fc06be559", "product": {"name": "discourse", "vendor": {"name": "discourse"}}, "product_version": "2026.1.0-latest, < 2026.1.8"}, {"id": "4a07c112-f05c-39ec-bb75-45ffded470f0", "product": {"name": "discourse", "vendor": {"name": "discourse"}}, "product_version": "2026.7.0-latest, < 2026.7.2"}, {"id": "f709bd51-99f7-33fe-8b31-961ca332d3ac", "product": {"name": "discourse", "vendor": {"name"